IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mca-nouns`
IMPORT `mca-act`

-- Minors' Contracts Act 1987 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 1 April 2022 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a minor, or a person who contracted with a minor, asking on facts they can state whether the Infants
-- Relief Act 1874 still stands in the way of their contract, whether a guarantee of the minor's obligation
-- survives, what property the court may make the minor hand back, and whether the Act has shut them out.
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in mca-act.l4 as the questions that person would ask.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no layer-1 module changes to suit it.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a date, or Yes / No / "I am not sure" -- one for
-- each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as they would be asked.  The records the long
-- module expects are built inside each question from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called.
--   * A fact that is law the Act presupposes ("the contract is unenforceable against the minor because they
--     were a minor"; "section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable") is asked as
--     Yes / No / "I am not sure"; "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that needs it answers NOTHING.
--     A person is never taken to have said No for a thing they do not know.
--   * No age is typed anywhere: whether a party was a minor is a fact the person states, because this Act does
--     not say at what age a person stops being a minor.
--   * Nobody can state the court's judgment that a transfer is "just and equitable"; they state their own view,
--     or "I am not sure".  The Act leaves the test to the court.
--
-- WHAT THIS ACT ANSWERS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT.  The Act does not say that a minor's contract binds the
-- minor, nor that it can or cannot be enforced against them, nor that it can be ratified: it says only that the
-- 1874 Act does not apply (s 1), that a guarantee is not unenforceable for that reason alone (s 2), that the
-- court may make a minor hand back property (s 3) and that, for contracts made between 9 April 1987 and
-- 12 November 1993, none of this applies unless the Civil Law Act 1909 s 5 already made it applicable (s 4).
-- Whether a contract binds a minor is the common law, which is not among the sources: nothing here answers it.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act
-- does not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Never read NOTHING
-- as no.
--
-- There is no seat for the court.  Where a provision addresses only the court (s 3(1), the power to require a
-- transfer), the rule is in layer 1 and the person meets it only through the questions below.

DECLARE `My answer` IS ONE OF
    Yes
    No
    `I am not sure`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the module's inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN Yes THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN No THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- The contract, from what the person says.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      minor IS A BOOLEAN
      unenforceable IS A `My answer`
      repudiated IS A BOOLEAN
      reason IS A `My answer`
      saving IS A `My answer`
GIVETH A `Contract with a minor`
`my contract from what I say` MEANS
    `Contract with a minor` WITH
        `day the contract was made` IS day -- input mapping
        `one party was a minor when the contract was made` IS minor -- input mapping
        `the obligation is unenforceable against that party` IS `what I say, as a fact` unenforceable -- input mapping
        `that party repudiates the contract` IS repudiated -- input mapping
        `that is because that party was a minor when the contract was made` IS `what I say, as a fact` reason -- input mapping
        `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made the provision applicable` IS `what I say, as a fact` saving -- input mapping

§ `The Minors' Contracts Act 1987 -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 still stand in the way of my contract? (s 1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 1.  The Infants Relief Act 1874 "shall not apply to any contract made by a minor after 9 April 1987".
-- The Act does not say the contract is valid, binding or ratified; it says only that the 1874 Act does not apply.
-- Nothing in the Act applies to a contract made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993 unless section
-- 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made it applicable (s 4): see the last group.  This question does not read the
-- minor's other facts (a fixed placeholder is used for each, and nothing reads it).
@export Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to the contract I made as a minor (s 1)?
GIVEN `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract made?
      `a party was a minor when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a party to the contract a minor (below the age of majority) when the contract was made?
      `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable` IS A `My answer` @desc If the contract was made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993: was this provision of the Act applicable to your contract by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 as in force before 12 November 1993? For a contract made on any other date it does not matter; answer I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` IS
    `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 applies to the contract` (`my contract from what I say` `the day the contract was made` `a party was a minor when it was made` `I am not sure` FALSE `I am not sure` `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable`)

-- s 1, first effect named in the bracket: the 1874 Act "invalidates certain contracts made by minors".
@export Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 make the contract I made as a minor invalid (s 1)?
GIVEN `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract made?
      `a party was a minor when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a party to the contract a minor (below the age of majority) when the contract was made?
      `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable` IS A `My answer` @desc If the contract was made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993: was this provision of the Act applicable to your contract by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 as in force before 12 November 1993? For a contract made on any other date it does not matter; answer I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 invalidate my contract` IS
    `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 invalidates the contract` (`my contract from what I say` `the day the contract was made` `a party was a minor when it was made` `I am not sure` FALSE `I am not sure` `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable`)

-- s 1, second effect named in the bracket: the 1874 Act "prohibits actions to enforce contracts ratified after majority".
@export If the contract I made as a minor is ratified after majority, does the Infants Relief Act 1874 stop an action to enforce it (s 1)?
GIVEN `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract made?
      `a party was a minor when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a party to the contract a minor (below the age of majority) when the contract was made?
      `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable` IS A `My answer` @desc If the contract was made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993: was this provision of the Act applicable to your contract by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 as in force before 12 November 1993? For a contract made on any other date it does not matter; answer I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 stop an action on my contract ratified after majority` IS
    `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 bars an action on the contract ratified after majority` (`my contract from what I say` `the day the contract was made` `a party was a minor when it was made` `I am not sure` FALSE `I am not sure` `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Is the guarantee of a minor's obligation still enforceable? (s 2)`
-- Situation: asked only of a person who holds, or has given, a guarantee of an obligation of a party who was a minor.
-- The form can ask "Has a guarantee been given for the minor's obligation?" before showing this group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 2.  Where a guarantee is given for an obligation of a party to a contract made after 9 April 1987, and the
-- obligation is unenforceable against him (or he repudiates the contract) because he was a minor, the
-- guarantee shall not for that reason alone be unenforceable against the guarantor.
@export Does section 2 save the guarantee of the minor's obligation from being unenforceable on that ground alone (s 2)?
GIVEN `a guarantee has been given for an obligation of a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc This question assumes that a party was a minor when the contract was made; if none was, it does not apply to you. Has a guarantee been given in respect of an obligation of a party to the contract?
      `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract made?
      `the obligation is unenforceable against the minor` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the obligation unenforceable against the minor? Say I am not sure if you have not been told.
      `the minor has repudiated the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the minor repudiated (disowned) the contract?
      `that is because the party was a minor` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the reason for that (the obligation being unenforceable, or the minor repudiating the contract) that the party was a minor when the contract was made? Say I am not sure if you do not know.
      `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable` IS A `My answer` @desc If the contract was made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993: was this provision of the Act applicable to your contract by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 as in force before 12 November 1993? For a contract made on any other date it does not matter; answer I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the guarantee saved` IS
    `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`Guarantee case` WITH `the contract guaranteed` IS `my contract from what I say` `the day the contract was made` TRUE `the obligation is unenforceable against the minor` `the minor has repudiated the contract` `that is because the party was a minor` `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable`, `a guarantee is given in respect of an obligation of a party to the contract` IS `a guarantee has been given for an obligation of a party to the contract`)

-- s 2, the tail of the section, from the guarantor's side as much as the lender's: can the guarantor refuse to
-- honour the guarantee only because the minor's obligation cannot be enforced against the minor?
@export Is the guarantee unenforceable against the guarantor only because the borrower was a minor (s 2)?
GIVEN `a guarantee has been given for an obligation of a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc This question assumes that a party was a minor when the contract was made; if none was, it does not apply to you. Has a guarantee been given in respect of an obligation of a party to the contract?
      `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract made?
      `the obligation is unenforceable against the minor` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the obligation unenforceable against the minor? Say I am not sure if you have not been told.
      `the minor has repudiated the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the minor repudiated (disowned) the contract?
      `that is because the party was a minor` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the reason for that (the obligation being unenforceable, or the minor repudiating the contract) that the party was a minor when the contract was made? Say I am not sure if you do not know.
      `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable` IS A `My answer` @desc If the contract was made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993: was this provision of the Act applicable to your contract by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 as in force before 12 November 1993? For a contract made on any other date it does not matter; answer I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the guarantee unenforceable only because the borrower was a minor` IS
    `s 2 the guarantee is unenforceable against the guarantor for that reason alone` (`Guarantee case` WITH `the contract guaranteed` IS `my contract from what I say` `the day the contract was made` TRUE `the obligation is unenforceable against the minor` `the minor has repudiated the contract` `that is because the party was a minor` `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable`, `a guarantee is given in respect of an obligation of a party to the contract` IS `a guarantee has been given for an obligation of a party to the contract`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Can the court make the minor hand back property? (s 3)`
-- Situation: asked only of a contract that is unenforceable against a party because he was a minor, or that the minor has repudiated.
-- The form can ask "Is the contract unenforceable against the minor, or has the minor repudiated it?" before showing this group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 3(1), from the other party's side: "the court may, if it is just and equitable to do so, require the
-- defendant to transfer to the claimant any property acquired by the defendant under the contract, or any
-- property representing it."  Yes means the court HAS the power; it does not say the court will use it.
@export Can the court make the minor transfer to me property the minor acquired under our contract (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `I entered into the contract with the minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc This question assumes that a party was a minor when the contract was made; if none was, it does not apply to you. Did you enter into the contract with the minor?
      `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract made?
      `the contract is unenforceable against the minor` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the contract unenforceable against the minor? Say I am not sure if you have not been told.
      `the minor has repudiated the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the minor repudiated (disowned) the contract?
      `that is because the minor was a minor` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the reason for that (the contract being unenforceable, or the minor repudiating it) that the minor was a minor when the contract was made? Say I am not sure if you do not know.
      `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable` IS A `My answer` @desc If the contract was made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993: was this provision of the Act applicable to your contract by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 as in force before 12 November 1993? For a contract made on any other date it does not matter; answer I am not sure.
      `the minor acquired the property under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the minor acquire the property under the contract?
      `the property represents property the minor acquired under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property something that stands in the place of property the minor acquired under the contract?
      `it is just and equitable that the minor transfer it` IS A `My answer` @desc In your view, is it just and equitable that the minor be made to transfer the property to you? The court decides; say I am not sure if you cannot say.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` IS
    `s 3(1) the court may require the defendant to transfer property to the claimant`
        (`Restitution case` WITH `the contract sued on` IS `my contract from what I say` `the day the contract was made` TRUE `the contract is unenforceable against the minor` `the minor has repudiated the contract` `that is because the minor was a minor` `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable`, `the claimant entered into the contract with the defendant` IS `I entered into the contract with the minor`)
        (Property OF `the minor acquired the property under the contract`, `the property represents property the minor acquired under the contract`)
        `the claimant`
        (`what I say, as a fact` `it is just and equitable that the minor transfer it`)

-- s 3(1), from the minor's side: the same rule, asked by the person it may be applied to.
@export Can the court make me, as the minor, transfer property I acquired under the contract to the other party (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `the other party entered into the contract with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc This question assumes that a party was a minor when the contract was made; if none was, it does not apply to you. Did the other party enter into the contract with you?
      `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract made?
      `the contract is unenforceable against me` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the contract unenforceable against you? Say I am not sure if you have not been told.
      `I have repudiated the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you repudiated (disowned) the contract?
      `that is because I was a minor` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the reason for that (the contract being unenforceable against you, or your repudiating it) that you were a minor when the contract was made? Say I am not sure if you do not know.
      `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable` IS A `My answer` @desc If the contract was made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993: was this provision of the Act applicable to your contract by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 as in force before 12 November 1993? For a contract made on any other date it does not matter; answer I am not sure.
      `I acquired the property under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire the property under the contract?
      `the property represents property I acquired under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property something that stands in the place of property you acquired under the contract?
      `it is just and equitable that I transfer it` IS A `My answer` @desc In your view, is it just and equitable that you be made to transfer the property to the other party? The court decides; say I am not sure if you cannot say.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` IS
    `s 3(1) the court may require the defendant to transfer property to the claimant`
        (`Restitution case` WITH `the contract sued on` IS `my contract from what I say` `the day the contract was made` TRUE `the contract is unenforceable against me` `I have repudiated the contract` `that is because I was a minor` `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable`, `the claimant entered into the contract with the defendant` IS `the other party entered into the contract with me`)
        (Property OF `I acquired the property under the contract`, `the property represents property I acquired under the contract`)
        `the claimant`
        (`what I say, as a fact` `it is just and equitable that I transfer it`)

-- s 3(1), the conditions alone: does the court's power exist at all for this contract?
@export Are the conditions for a restitution order under section 3(1) met for my contract?
GIVEN `the other party entered into the contract with the minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc This question assumes that a party was a minor when the contract was made; if none was, it does not apply to you. Did the claimant (the person who is asking the court for the property) enter into the contract with the minor?
      `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract made?
      `the contract is unenforceable against the minor` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the contract unenforceable against the minor? Say I am not sure if you have not been told.
      `the minor has repudiated the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the minor repudiated (disowned) the contract?
      `that is because the minor was a minor` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the reason for that (the contract being unenforceable, or the minor repudiating it) that the minor was a minor when the contract was made? Say I am not sure if you do not know.
      `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable` IS A `My answer` @desc If the contract was made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993: was this provision of the Act applicable to your contract by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 as in force before 12 November 1993? For a contract made on any other date it does not matter; answer I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the conditions for the restitution order met` IS
    `s 3(1) the conditions for the court's power are met` (`Restitution case` WITH `the contract sued on` IS `my contract from what I say` `the day the contract was made` TRUE `the contract is unenforceable against the minor` `the minor has repudiated the contract` `that is because the minor was a minor` `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable`, `the claimant entered into the contract with the defendant` IS `the other party entered into the contract with the minor`)

-- s 3(2): "Nothing in this section shall be taken to prejudice any other remedy available to the claimant."
-- No: using section 3 does not cost the other party their other remedies.
@export Does section 3 prejudice any other remedy I have against the minor (s 3(2))?
GIVEN `I entered into the contract with the minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc This question assumes that a party was a minor when the contract was made; if none was, it does not apply to you. Did you enter into the contract with the minor?
      `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract made?
      `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable` IS A `My answer` @desc If the contract was made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993: was this provision of the Act applicable to your contract by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 as in force before 12 November 1993? For a contract made on any other date it does not matter; answer I am not sure.
      `the remedy is something other than asking the court for a transfer under section 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the remedy you have in mind something other than asking the court for a transfer of property under section 3(1)?
      `the remedy is available to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that remedy available to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 3 prejudice my other remedy` IS
    `s 3(2) this section prejudices another remedy available to the claimant`
        (`Restitution case` WITH `the contract sued on` IS `my contract from what I say` `the day the contract was made` TRUE `I am not sure` FALSE `I am not sure` `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable`, `the claimant entered into the contract with the defendant` IS `I entered into the contract with the minor`)
        (Remedy OF `the remedy is something other than asking the court for a transfer under section 3(1)`, `the remedy is available to me`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Is the Minors' Contracts Act shut out of my contract? (s 4)`
-- Situation: asked only of a contract made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993.
-- The form can ask "Was your contract made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993?" before showing this group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 4.  "Nothing in this Act applies in relation to a contract made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November
-- 1993 except in so far as it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in force before
-- 12 November 1993."  Yes: the Act is shut out.  No: s 4 does not shut it out, because the exception is met or because
-- the contract was made outside the window the text names (on or before 9 April 1987, or on or after 12 November
-- 1993).  NOTHING: you do not know whether section 5 made the Act applicable.
@export Is the Minors' Contracts Act 1987 shut out of my contract by section 4?
GIVEN `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract made?
      `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable` IS A `My answer` @desc If the contract was made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993: was the provision of the Act you are asking about applicable to your contract by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 as in force before 12 November 1993? For a contract made on any other date it does not matter; answer I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Act shut out of my contract` IS
    `s 4 this Act is barred from applying to the contract` (`my contract from what I say` `the day the contract was made` TRUE `I am not sure` FALSE `I am not sure` `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable`)
